        {
            "id": 18,
            "type": "text",
            "title": "Fair Scheduling Validation",
            "gridPos": {
                "x": 0,
                "y": 69,
                "w": 24,
                "h": 8
            },
            "options": {
                "mode": "markdown",
                "content": "### Fairness is intentionally not a Prometheus metric\n\nValidate this with the load-test harness using the **actual claim sequence**:\n\n1. Capture `user_id` for each claimed job in the test harness.\n2. Compute per-user **service share**.\n3. Measure **maximum consecutive claims** by one user.\n4. Measure each user's **maximum scheduling gap / queue wait**.\n5. Check for **starvation violations**.\n\nDo **not** add `user_id` as a Prometheus label. High-cardinality per-user metrics are not needed to prove the scheduler's fairness property.\n\nA useful test workload is several active users with deliberately different queue depths. The expected property is that a continuously backlogged user does not monopolize the worker while other active users have work waiting."
            }
        },
